  "readmeFile": "ReadmeNuget.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- Scripts: functions can now be declared static and module-level constants can be declared with const. Other modules can call them as ModuleName.Function() / ModuleName.Constant (module name identifiers expose only static members; const values are primitives, strings and design enums, evaluated once per module in declaration order).\n- New field ListUpDownButtonField: a vertical move-up / move-down button pair to place inside a ListField row layout (custom DetailLayoutName cells). It moves the parent list row internally, disables itself at the first / last row and keeps keyboard focus after the move.\n- ListField: fixed row move up / down for rows without an Id (rows are now located by reference instead of Id text), affecting both the standard buttons and ListUpDownButtonField.\n- RecordPagingField: fetching the neighbouring page when crossing a page boundary now selects only the Id column instead of the full list columns and linked data.\n- DetailListField / TileListField: the row actions (move up / move down / delete) are now small icon buttons overlaid at the top-right corner of each card, faded until the card is hovered, selected or focused. The TileListField \"Add\" button is rendered as a short dashed slot below the tiles. Colors are driven by the Bootstrap --bs-btn-* variables so they can still be customised from app.css via [data-system=\"delete\"] etc.\n- Components: BooleanField (toggle), LinkField, ListField, DetailListField and TileListField no longer hard-code colors (validation red, selected-row background, cell button border); they use the Bootstrap theme variables (--bs-form-invalid-*, --bs-primary-rgb, --bs-border-color) so custom themes and dark mode are respected.\n- [Designer] attribute can now be applied to enum members (AttributeTargets.Field) to provide a localized DisplayName; all design enums (ButtonVariant, HorizontalAlignment, MatchComparison, ...) carry such names.",
